<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy — Where Is Baldo?" description="Cookie Policy for whereisbaldo.com">
  <div class="post-header">
    <span class="post-tag">Legal</span>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="post-meta">Effective Date: May 2026 · whereisbaldo.com</p>
  </div>
  <div class="post-body legal-body">

    <h2>What Are Cookies?</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help websites remember your preferences, understand how you use the site, and serve relevant content and advertising.</p>

    <h2>Cookies This Site Uses</h2>
    <p><strong>Essential Cookies</strong> — These are necessary for the website to function properly. They cannot be disabled.</p>
    <p><strong>Analytics Cookies (Google Analytics)</strong> — We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors interact with this site — which pages are popular, where traffic comes from, and how long people stay. This data is anonymous and helps us improve the content we produce. Google Analytics uses cookies including <code>_ga</code>, <code>_gid</code>, and <code>_gat</code>. These cookies do not identify you personally.</p>
    <p><strong>Advertising Cookies (Google AdSense)</strong> — This site displays ads through Google AdSense. Google uses cookies to show you ads that are relevant to your interests based on your browsing activity across websites. These cookies are set by Google, not by this site. You can manage your Google ad preferences at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">google.com/settings/ads</a>.</p>

    <h2>Third-Party Cookies</h2>
    <p>Some content or features on this site may be provided by third parties (such as embedded videos or social media buttons). These third parties may set their own cookies. We do not control these cookies and recommend reviewing the privacy policies of any third-party services you interact with.</p>

    <h2>How to Control Cookies</h2>
    <p>You can control and manage cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers allow you to view what cookies are stored, delete cookies individually or all at once, block cookies from specific sites, and block all third-party cookies. Note that disabling certain cookies may affect how this site functions.</p>
    <p>Browser cookie settings: <a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chrome</a> · <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Firefox</a> · <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Safari</a> · <a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/microsoft-edge-browsing-data-and-privacy-bb8174ba-9d73-dcf2-9b4a-c582b4e640dd" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Edge</a></p>

    <h2>Opting Out of Analytics and Ads</h2>
    <p><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> Install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out Add-on</a>.<br />
    <strong>Personalized ads:</strong> Visit <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ad Settings</a> or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Your Online Choices</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Cookie Policy as we add new features or tools. The effective date at the top reflects the most recent update.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? <strong><a href="mailto:baldolanded@gmail.com">baldolanded@gmail.com</a></strong></p>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-body h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
